{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You shall burn with fire.</b> We find no outer sin-offering burned except this one. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 29:14). And it was a temporary ruling, according to the words of our Sages. And the reason for this is that all is revealed before Him, and this bull of sin-offering was to atone for the deed of the calf, and the offering of the anointed priest is it (Leviticus 4:3). And there (Leviticus 4:6) He commands to bring its blood inside to the curtain, but He did not wish now to bring it in there, to the inner part, because there (4:6) it says in the reason \"in front of the curtain of the sanctuary,\" but here the sanctuary had not yet been sanctified and the Shekhinah had not yet dwelt upon it that it would be called \"the curtain of the sanctuary,\" and behold the outer is like the inner. And the leaning of the hands upon his sons — because He was angered at Aaron to destroy him (Deuteronomy 9:20), and it was an atonement through his sons (Leviticus Rabbah 7:1) — they too were required to obtain atonement through it. And the reason for the burning is like the reason for the burning of the red heifer, and its secret is known from the goat sent away:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The closing phrase וסודה ידוע מן השעיר המשתלח ('and its secret is known from the goat sent away') is left without further explanation, consistent with Ramban's practice of cryptic kabbalistic allusion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:19:10.137006046Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}